  "body": "## What changed (Part 1 of 2)\n\nRTK (Rust Token Killer) integration core — a single source of truth plus a reconciler.\n\n- `config/rtk.py` — `RtkState {claude, codex, pi}` in `~/.fcc/rtk.json` (atomic, corrupt-tolerant); `apply_rtk_state()` runs `rtk init -g --auto-patch|--codex|--agent pi` / `rtk init --uninstall ...` to reconcile; `_ensure_rtk_binary()` downloads the pinned 0.44.2 release, SHA-256 verifies, extracts to `~/.local/bin/rtk`. All calls set `RTK_TELEMETRY_DISABLED=1`.\n- `cli/rtk_commands.py` — `mcc-rtk`/`fcc-rtk` with `status`/`enable`/`disable`/`uninstall`/`apply`.\n- Installers gain `--rtk`/`-Rtk` → enables all three agents after install.\n\n## Why not a straight upstream port\n\nOur installers are wheel-only (the agent-install/select subsystem was removed), so upstream's \"configure RTK per selected agent\" had nothing to hang on. This instead gives RTK a persistent state + reconciler, with management surfaces coming in Part 2.\n\n## Verification\n\n- 48 new RTK tests; full suite **4049 passed / 6 failed** (6 = pre-existing PowerShell-installer baseline).\n- `ruff format --check`, `ruff check`, `ty check`: clean.\n\n## Residual risks\n\n- No live end-to-end RTK round-trip in CI (RTK binary isn't installed on runners); download/verify/extract and command dispatch are unit-tested with fakes.\n- Part 2 (dashboard + desktop toggles) lands next.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
