    "message": "feat(rtk): RTK token-optimizer state model, reconciler, CLI, and installer flag\n\nPart 1 of 2. Adds the RTK (Rust Token Killer) integration core — a single source\nof truth plus a reconciler that makes the machine match it.\n\n- config/rtk.py: RtkState {claude, codex, pi} persisted to ~/.fcc/rtk.json\n  (atomic, corrupt-tolerant); apply_rtk_state() reconciles by running\n  `rtk init -g --auto-patch|--codex|--agent pi` / `rtk init --uninstall ...`;\n  _ensure_rtk_binary() downloads the pinned 0.44.2 release, checksum-verifies,\n  and extracts to ~/.local/bin/rtk (tar.gz/zip per platform). All invocations\n  set RTK_TELEMETRY_DISABLED=1.\n- cli/rtk_commands.py: mcc-rtk / fcc-rtk with status/enable/disable/uninstall/apply.\n- Installers gain --rtk / -Rtk, which enables all three agents after install.\n- identity.py + entrypoints.py register the new command family.\n\nVerification: 48 new RTK tests + full suite 4049 passed / 6 pre-existing\nPS-installer failures (baseline unchanged); ruff format/check + ty clean.\n\nPart 2 (dashboard + desktop toggles) follows in a separate PR.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
